# Grok Viral dashboard — Scriptify v3, conformed to 02.mp4
# npx tsx scripts/vo.ts scripts/vo/grok-viral-dashboard.vo

## Hook

A post in your niche pulled 2,158 likes last week, and 5,834 saves.
You never saw it, because native analytics only cover your own posts, and trend pages only show you what already peaked.
So we're building a Grok Bot that scrapes X, TikTok, and Instagram overnight and ranks them by save rate before you're awake.
Here's how.

[pause 0.5]

## Setup

Grok Bot is xAI's always-on agent app, and the reason we're using it here is that it keeps working after you close your laptop.
Open its marketplace, install the Apify plugin, and sign in once.
That plugin brings Apify MCP server and a set of scraping skills with it, which is what lets you run any Actor in Apify Store by asking rather than by writing code.

[pause 0.4]

## The prompt

Then give the bot one prompt.
Run Tweet Scraper on your search terms sorted by Top, TikTok Scraper with your search queries against the video section, and Instagram Scraper on your tag pages.
Before it normalizes anything, have it show you which engagement fields each Actor returned.

[pause 0.4]

## Field mapping

That last instruction is the one that decides whether this bot is worth anything.
You're not checking post counts, you're checking what each platform actually calls the number you care about.
Tweet Scraper returns saves as bookmark count.
TikTok Scraper calls likes digg count, and saves collect count.
Instagram Scraper gives you likes count and comments count, and no save count at all.
Same human action, three different names, and one platform missing the best signal entirely.
Skip this and let the agent guess, and you get a board that ranks TikTok above X because one platform counted plays where the other counted impressions.

[pause 0.4]

## Instagram

Instagram needs a decision, not a guess.
Since there's no public save count, we substitute comments divided by likes, and we label that column separately so nobody reads an Instagram row as a save.

[pause 0.4]

## Build

Now let it build.
It normalizes all three into one table of platform, likes, saves, and views, drops anything under 24 hours old, ranks by save rate, and renders a page where every row links back to the original post.

[pause 0.4]

## Filters

Watch what the filters actually do.
This run kept 128 posts.
It dropped four for being under a day old, and 18 more for having no usable save rate.
Both of those matter for the same reason: tag pages come back newest first, so some of what you scrape is minutes old with nothing on it yet, and a post with no save count can't be ranked by save rate at all.
Leave either filter out and your number one row is noise.

[pause 0.5]

## Top three

Here's the payoff.
Top three by save rate: the leader has 2,158 likes and 5,834 saves, a rate of 2.7.
Second place, 1,104 likes and 2,841 saves.
Third, 593 likes and 1,488 saves.
Likes tell you a post was enjoyed.
Saves tell you someone intends to come back and do the thing.

[pause 0.4]

## Standing

A page you have to remember to open is still work, so make it standing.
Set a weekday digest, and the bot re-scrapes and re-ranks every morning on its own.

[pause 0.4]

## Telegram

Then get it off your laptop.
Create a Telegram bot with BotFather, copy the token, install the Composio plugin in Grok Bot, and connect it.
One gotcha worth knowing: a Telegram bot can't message you first, so send it any message once, and after that it can push.
Tell it to send the top three rows with the save rate and the link, and nothing else.
A bot that sends 20 rows gets muted in a week.
A bot that sends three gets read.

[pause 0.5]

## Outro

That's the real shift.
You're not building a dashboard, you're adding a teammate who's awake when a post starts moving and has it ranked by the time you sit down.

[pause 0.3]

The next time a post in your niche pulls nearly three times more saves than likes, you don't miss it.
It's in your messages before you're awake, with the save rate and the link.
To build yours, create an Apify account from the link below, install the Apify plugin in Grok Bot, and start with Tweet Scraper.
